# Intent: The approved face design on the unit (owner brief 2026-11-16: Big eyes had become plain white circles; the approved design board shows the anime look). Every style but Stock now draws the design board's face: a rounded eye box per style (Big eyes 96 by 104, Eyes only 84 by 88 at radius 55 percent, Classic 56 by 72 at 90, Minimal 28 by 40); Big eyes adds a large pupil (37 percent of the short side) that follows the gaze 1.3 times as far as the eye does, with two highlights, masked by the eye (a ring in the screen colour, 18 px, only while the pupil leaves the eye) so a big look cuts it to a crescent; the lid is a straight edge over the eye (the fraction of the height it covers, tilted by the emotion's slant) and the happy cheek is an ellipse rising from below (strips, so it is a true ellipse); the lid strip is clipped at the eye's top so an angry corner never folds over; a blink lowers the height to 3 percent and widens by 6 percent (55 ms shut, 85 ms open); brows (angry, sad, doubt, surprised, thinking) in Big eyes and Classic; hearts for love; closed arcs for sleeping; the thinking look (up and away, lid low, right eye smaller, no mouth) while the dots show; the mouth is one curve (width, curve, tilt, offset) that fills into a lens when open, speaking opens it at 38 ms and closes it at 105 ms, Eyes only pulses its eyes 14 percent with the voice; dots are 13 px, 26 apart, low on the face; gaze drift is the style's amplitude (6, 8, 5, 6 px), the pupil follows; one damped spring (k 420, ratio 0.62, about 8 percent overshoot, settled in 350 ms) eases every pose value, one shared lid and one shared blink for both eyes. One definition: hal/maipai_look_core.h holds the table (ml_spec, ml_pose_target), the spring and the shape builders (ml_eye_shapes, ml_brow_shapes, ml_mouth_lens); the unit, the host renderer and the settings page preview draw those shapes. Stock is drawn exactly as before (pixel for pixel, checked on the host renderer). Left and right eyes are identical about their centres at rest (measured 0.0 px apart over ten rest frames in every style). Cost: two eye objects and two brow objects replace the circle and lid boxes; the shapes (at most 48 of 40 bytes) are built per frame on the stack and compared, only what changed is invalidated (rest, Big eyes: about 9 thousand pixels a frame on average against 1 thousand before; a gaze move redraws about 20 thousand; an emotion change about 45 thousand for 0.4 s; measured by flushed pixels on the host renderer, PERF=1; the unit's frame time is not measured).
# Placement: unit (the face runs on the robot, so it is complete with no host)
# Upstream: firmware/main/stackchan/avatar/skins/default/{default.h,default.cpp,eyes.cpp,mouth.cpp} of the StackChan main component (MIT) as rebuilt by patch X01; hal/maipai_look_core.h of X01
